2.4  Redistribute the Software Unmodified and in full, with this licence and all
     notices intact. This is what makes it lawful to install a published package
     from a registry, pull a published container image, or mirror either
     internally.

2.5  Modify your own copy, for your own deployment, provided the result is never
     distributed, published, sold or otherwise made available to anyone outside
     your organisation, and is not offered to third parties as a service
     distinguishable from the Unmodified Software.

     This exists so that nobody has to wait for the Licensor to fix a
     vulnerability, adjust a log level, or stop an incident. It is not a general
